# Execution Plans

Copy this file to `PLANS.md` when the repository uses multi-hour or
multi-session execution plans. Store active plans in the project-designated
location, for example `plans/<change-id>.md`.

<!-- PORTABLE_PLAN_TEMPLATE -->

Remove this marker when adopting the file.

An execution plan is a self-contained living document. A new contributor must
be able to resume the work from the plan, repository, and recorded evidence
without relying on missing conversation history.

This is the only detailed implementation plan for a change. When formal
governance is enabled, `DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md` stores approval metadata and links
to this file; do not duplicate progress, decisions, steps, or verification in
both places.

Continue the same plan only for the same unfinished observable outcome. Use a
new Change ID and a new plan for a materially different, closed, released, or
independently approved outcome. If implementation reveals a behavior, design,
or acceptance-test change, record the discovery, pause delivery work, update
the governed source and approval digests, and obtain the required renewed
approval before continuing. Isolated exploration is not deliverable
implementation or acceptance evidence.

## Required Plan Sections

```markdown
# {{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}} {{REPLACE_ME:ACTION_ORIENTED_OUTCOME}}

## Purpose and Observable Outcome
{{REPLACE_ME:PURPOSE_AND_OBSERVABLE_OUTCOME}}

## Context and Constraints
{{REPLACE_ME:CONTEXT_AND_CONSTRAINTS}}

<!-- SDD_APPROVED_PLAN_BASIS_BEGIN -->
## Approved Plan Basis

### Requirement Coverage
{{REPLACE_ME:REQUIREMENT_COVERAGE}}

### Technical Design
{{REPLACE_ME:TECHNICAL_DESIGN}}

### Task Breakdown
| Task ID | Requirement IDs | Dependencies | Files/components | Verification |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| TASK-{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}}-001 | REQ-{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}}-001 | none | {{REPLACE_ME:FILES_OR_COMPONENTS}} | TEST-{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}}-001 |

### Verification Basis
{{REPLACE_ME:VERIFICATION_BASIS}}
<!-- SDD_APPROVED_PLAN_BASIS_END -->

## Progress
- [ ] {{REPLACE_ME:TIMESTAMPED_PROGRESS}}

## Surprises and Discoveries
- {{REPLACE_ME:SURPRISES_AND_DISCOVERIES}}

## Decision Log
- {{REPLACE_ME:DECISION_LOG}}

## Recovery and Idempotence
{{REPLACE_ME:RECOVERY_AND_IDEMPOTENCE}}

## Outcomes and Retrospective
{{REPLACE_ME:OUTCOMES_AND_RETROSPECTIVE}}
```

Update `Progress`, discoveries, decisions, and verification at every meaningful
stopping point. Do not mark an item complete based only on an implementation
claim; record the observable evidence. Never place secrets or sensitive
production data in a plan.

For each material uncertainty, record the issue and evidence, viable options,
their consequences, the recommended option and rationale, and the named
decision owner. Record the owner's actual decision separately; do not present a
recommendation as approval.

For required SDD, the bytes from `SDD_APPROVED_PLAN_BASIS_BEGIN` through
`SDD_APPROVED_PLAN_BASIS_END` form the approved plan basis. Do not edit that
block after approval without recalculating its digest and obtaining renewed
approval. Living progress, discoveries, decisions, and outcomes remain outside
the block and may be updated without changing the approved basis.
